//? Title: Tricubic interpolation: the actual64-sample neighborhood
//? Subtitle: Actual native state, retained fixtures and explicit limits
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A sampled three-dimensional field must be evaluated between grid points.
Separable cubic convolution blends64 nearby samples, with explicit validation
and a stated boundary extension.
)

\toc

> The method

With Keys kernel a=−1/2, w(t)=(a+2)|t|³−(a+3)|t|²+1 for |t|≤1,
a|t|³−5a|t|²+8a|t|−4a for1<|t|<2, and0 otherwise. The3D interpolant sums
w(tx−l)w(ty−m)w(tz−n)V over l,m,n∈{−1,0,1,2}. Interior weights reproduce
constants and linear coordinates; their tensor product reproduces trilinear
fields. At boundaries, repeated edge samples change that reproduction property.
Negative weights permit overshoot, so this is not a range-preserving
interpolator.

> Simple worked example

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/tricubic_interpolation_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <numeric>
#include <numbers>
#include <random>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
#include <map>
#include <set>
#include <array>
#include <tuple>
#include <bit>
#include <datamunge/random/quality.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/tricubic_interpolation.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    std::vector<double> axis{0, 1, 2, 3}, v(64);
    std::iota(v.begin(), v.end(), 0.);
    auto r = a::tricubic_work(axis, axis, axis, v, 1.5, 1.5, 1.5);
    std::print("| actual result | actual sample reads | weight sum |\n|---:|---:|---:|\n|{}|{}|{}|\n",
               r.value, r.indices.size(),
               std::accumulate(r.weights.begin(), r.weights.end(), 0.));
    std::print("\nFlattened field16x+4y+z gives31.5 at the centre.\n");
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0}, "Interior query 1.5,1.5,1.5");
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0},
                         std::format("{} actual weighted samples",
                                     r.indices.size()));
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0}, std::format("Actual value {}", r.value));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/tricubic_interpolation_tiny.svg");
}
```
