> Interpretation and limits

Queries must lie inside finite uniformly spaced axes; complete shape and finite
sample validation precedes index conversion. The query performs64 sample reads,
but the convenience call also validates the complete volume. A boundary error
curve is not evidence for a uniform interior convergence order.

Every figure is saved locally by its complete editable program. No separate
reconstruction supplies algorithm state. Counters describe the selected events,
not elapsed time or peak memory.

> References

